.UPDATE...
Issued at 941 AM PDT Mon Aug 3 2026

Satellite imagery this morning and current windfield along the
coast shows a semi-southerly surge. Low clouds continue to sneak
farther north up the coast near Pt Reyes. We even see a few
clouds up the Salinas Valley. Inland clouds will roll back to the
coast by this afternoon, but clouds will linger along the coast.
As noted below the bigger weather impact for today will be the
Heat. No update with current Heat Advisories as they remain valid
for interior N and E Bay. Finally, one other highlight this
morning with the southerly surge is what`s happening above the
surge.  over the higher terrain showed critically low humidity
with several sites in the single digits. This is a solid example
of nocturnal drying where humidity recovers early in the night
then dry toward sunrise. Therefore, critical fire weather
conditions exist.

No update need this morning, but will be monitoring the heat and
fire weather conditions through the day.

