.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1155 PM PDT Sun Aug 2 2026
(Tuesday night through next Sunday)

Upper level high pressure gradually builds into the region this
week. Flow becomes a bit more onshore each day, with the marine
layer trying to deepen to around 500-1000ft by Wednesday. This
should allow temperatures to gradually step down for the next two-
three days, with a warming trend returning for the late portion of
the work week. Widespread Moderate HeatRisk returns, with perhaps a
few patches of Major Heatrisk in the East and South Bay if the
trends holds. For now, confidence is too low to issue any sort of
heat products that far out but it will be something to watch over
the next day or so.

